#* {{quote-book|en|author=Joyce Farrell|title=Programming Logic & Design|year=2017|publisher=Cengage Learning|page=88|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=zqj5DQAAQBAJ&pg=PT113&dq=%22spaghetti+code%22&hl=&cd=3&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22spaghetti%20code%22&f=false|isbn=978-1-337-51704-1|passage=The descriptive name for logically snarled program statements is '''spaghetti code''', because the logic is as hard to follow as one noodle through a plate of spaghetti. Not only is '''spaghetti code''' confusing, but also the programs that contain it are prone to error, difficult to reuse, and hard to use as building blocks for larger applications.}}

